---
import { languages } from '../data/site';
---

<section class="border-b border-border">
  <div class="mx-auto grid w-full max-w-[1120px] gap-12 px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_360px] lg:gap-16">
    <div class="max-w-[720px]">
      <h2 class="text-[20px]">Built on ICPAC's ecosystem</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground sm:text-[16px]">
        ICPAC already produces the regional science: seasonal forecasts, the SPI drought
        index, subnational trigger thresholds and the digilib data catalogue. HALI
        consumes that work rather than duplicating it. Five layers from ICPAC's own
        GeoPortal render directly inside the HALI map, composited over HALI's alert
        zones, and the digilib SPI adapter is written and ready behind its flag.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground sm:text-[16px]">
        What HALI adds is the last mile. It takes regional analysis and turns it into a
        message in Afar or Luganda, with guidance specific to a pastoralist or a
        fisherfolk household, delivered on a feature phone with no account. The
        community reports that come back feed spatial clustering, which is where a
        regional trigger system gets ground truth it would otherwise wait for.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="self-start rounded-lg border border-border bg-card p-5">
      <h3 class="font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-muted-foreground">
        Languages per alert
      </h3>
      <ul class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
        {
          languages.map((lang) => (
            <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 text-[14px]">
              <code class="font-mono text-[12px] text-figure">{lang.code}</code>
              <span class="text-muted-foreground">{lang.name}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-5 border-t border-border pt-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        Tigrinya, Luganda and Afar are low-resource for current models. Output below the
        clarity floor is replaced with English and marked, rather than shipped wrong.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>
